4 Technical Details

4.1 MuJoCo Model
The simulation uses a MuJoCo XML model that includes:
&lt;!-- Example MuJoCo model structure (placeholder) --&gt;
&lt;mujoco model="golf_swing"&gt;
  &lt;worldbody&gt;
    &lt;body name="torso"&gt;
      &lt;!-- Torso geometry and inertia --&gt;
      &lt;geom type="cylinder" size="0.15 0.3"/&gt;
      &lt;joint name="torso_rotation" type="hinge"/&gt;

      &lt;body name="upper_arm"&gt;
        &lt;!-- Arm segment --&gt;
        &lt;geom type="capsule" size="0.04 0.3"/&gt;
        &lt;joint name="shoulder" type="ball"/&gt;

        &lt;body name="forearm"&gt;
          &lt;!-- Forearm segment --&gt;
          &lt;geom type="capsule" size="0.03 0.25"/&gt;
          &lt;joint name="elbow" type="hinge"/&gt;

          &lt;body name="hand"&gt;
            &lt;!-- Hand and club --&gt;
            &lt;geom type="box" size="0.05 0.03 0.1"/&gt;
            &lt;joint name="wrist" type="universal"/&gt;
          &lt;/body&gt;
        &lt;/body&gt;
      &lt;/body&gt;
    &lt;/body&gt;
  &lt;/worldbody&gt;
&lt;/mujoco&gt;


4.2 Physics Parameters
The model incorporates:

Segment masses based on anthropometric data
Inertia tensors for each body segment
Joint limits matching physiological constraints
Contact dynamics for club-ball interaction

